1. Stored Procedure Source Code Disclosure
Objective

Check whether application/business logic can be viewed.

Query
select name
from sysobjects
where type='P'
and (
      name like '%Party%'
   or name like '%Account%'
)

Then:

sp_helptext <procedure_name>
Finding

Stored Procedure Source Code Disclosure

Impact

Business logic, SQL queries, and sensitive table references become visible to non-administrative users.

2. Cross-Database Authorization Review
Objective

Determine whether your access extends beyond the intended database.

Query
use admin
go
select top 10 name from sysobjects
use cdaccess
go
select top 10 name from sysobjects
use d2query
go
select top 10 name from sysobjects
Finding

Excessive Cross-Database Read Permissions

Impact

A compromise of one account could expose data from multiple databases.

